  "id": "Compound::DB00957 - Gene::2099",
  "verbalization": "Norgestimate, a progestin analog, is linked to Esr1 through a shared pathway involving progestin and steroid classes. The evidence suggests that Norgestimate, as part of the Progesterone Congeners group, binds to Esr1 through a mechanism that involves steroid interactions. This is supported by the presence of multiple progestin derivatives—Ethynodiol, Desogestrel, and Etonogestrel—all of which are included in the Progesterone Congeners category and bind to Esr1. The lowest common ancestors of Norgestimate and these derivatives are both classified as Progestin and Steroid, indicating a common biological pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, mechanistically linked relationship, where Norgestimate's structural similarity to progestins facilitates its interaction with Esr1. The integration of these pathways highlights a general mechanism of steroid-based signaling, where progestin analogs may modulate ESR1 activity through shared molecular interactions.",
